[Term]
id: PSO:0000723
name: wheat dwarf bunt fungal disease
def: "A wheat disease caused by a Tilletia controversa affecting a plant structure." [AUTO:patterns/disease]
comment: Only impacts winter wheat; prolonged period of snow cover required for fungal germination; dark-colored bunt spores replace kernels; bunt spores give fishy odor; tiller number increases; plants become shorter ("dwarfed").
synonym: "dwarf smut" EXACT []
synonym: "stinking smut" EXACT []
xref: APSNET:Wheat
