[Term]
id: PSO:0000725
name: wheat eyespot fungal disease
def: "A wheat disease caused by a Oculimacula yallundae affecting a stem base." [AUTO:patterns/disease]
comment: Symptoms and signs:  The fungus infects stem base producing elliptical lessions of "eye" shapes. yellowish brown to tan brown and oriented lengthwise with the stem. A diagnotic weft of gray mycelium sometimes appears in the lumen of the stem beneath a lession.
synonym: "foot rot" EXACT []
synonym: "strawbreaker" EXACT []
xref: APSNET:Wheat
