[Term]
id: PSO:0000740
name: wheat take-all fungal disease
def: "A wheat disease caused by a Gaeumannomyces graminis affecting a plant structure." [AUTO:patterns/disease]
comment: Early stunting and foliar discoloration; limited tillering; bleached or straw-colored plants; limited formation of spikes; bleached spikes with shriveled kernels; dry rot of roots, crown, and basal culm tissue; shiny dark-brown to black surface mat of fungal tissue underneath leaf sheath at plant base; diseased plants easily pulled up from ground.
xref: APSNET:Wheat
