property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor "PSO:cooperl" xsd:string

[Term]
id: PSO:0000742
name: wheat sharp eyespot fungal disease
def: "A wheat disease caused by a Ceratobasidium cereale affecting a plant structure." [AUTO:patterns/disease]
comment: Bare patches in field; areas of uneven plant height; stunted plants; reduced root mass with pinched or constricted appearance; fine, sharp-looking, red-brown points on roots
synonym: "bare patch" EXACT []
xref: APSNET:Wheat
