[Term]
id: PSO:0000744
name: wheat barley yellow dwarf viral disease
def: "A wheat disease caused by a Barley yellow dwarf virus affecting a vascular leaf." [AUTO:patterns/disease]
comment: Symptoms: The quintessential symptoms are yellowing of leaves, especially the flag leaves and the shortening of internodes, resulting in a yellowed, dwarf plant. However, the discoloration can range across greens, yellows, oranges, reds, purples, and browns.
synonym: "cereal yellow dwarf" EXACT []
synonym: "WBYDV" EXACT []
xref: APSNET:Wheat
intersection_of: PSO:0000013 ! plant disease
