intersection_of: RO:0014001 NCBITaxon:12037
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor "0000-0002-9013-5974" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor "PSO:cooperl" xsd:string

[Term]
id: PSO:0000745
name: wheat soilborne mosaic viral disease
def: "A wheat disease caused by a Soil-borne wheat mosaic virus affecting a plant structure." [AUTO:patterns/disease]
comment: Symptoms: Infection occurs in roots, and symptoms appear on leaves. The natural mode of infection of wheat by SBWMV is transmitted by Polymyxa graminis, a soilborne plasmodiophoraceous organism. Symptoms range from mild green to prominent yellow leaf mosaics
synonym: "SBWMV" EXACT []
xref: APSNET:Wheat
intersection_of: PSO:0000013 ! plant disease
intersection_of: RO:0002162 NCBITaxon:4565
intersection_of: RO:0004025 PO:0009011
intersection_of: RO:0014001 NCBITaxon:28375
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor "0000-0002-9013-5974" xsd:string
property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor "PSO:cooperl" xsd:string

[Term]
id: PSO:0000746
name: wheat streak mosaic viral disease
def: "A wheat disease caused by a Wheat streak mosaic virus affecting a vascular leaf." [AUTO:patterns/disease]
comment: Symptoms:WSMV is transmitted by its mite vector. The margins of fields are often the first and sometimes the only areas affected. Infected plants usually are stunted and have mottled and streaked leaves. Leaf streaks are greenish yellow, parallel, and discontinuous.
synonym: "WSMV" EXACT []
xref: APSNET:Wheat
